Inspection ID: UnnecessaryContinue

fullDescription.text:
Reports array declarations written in C-style syntax, where the array brackets are placed after a variable name or after a method parameter list. Most code styles prefer Java-style array declarations, where the array brackets are placed after the type name. Example: 'public String process(String value[])[] {
    return value;
  }' After the quick-fix is applied: 'public String[] process(String[] value) {
    return value;
  }' Configure the inspection: Use the Ignore C-style declarations in variables option to report C-style array declaration of method return types only. Inspection ID: CStyleArrayDeclaration

