fullDescription.text:
Reports integer multiplications and left shifts that are implicitly cast to long. Example: 'void f(int i) {
    long val = 65536 * i;
  }' After the quick-fix is applied, the code changes to: 'void x(int i) {
    long val = 65536L * i;
  }' Example: 'void f(int i) {
    long value = i << 24;
  }' After the quick-fix is applied, the code changes to: 'void f(int i) {
    long value = (long) i << 24;
  }' Such multiplications are often a mistake, as overflow truncation may occur unexpectedly. Converting an 'int' literal to a 'long' literal ('65536L') fixes the problem. Inspection ID: IntegerMultiplicationImplicitCastToLong

