  if (condition2) return false;
  return true;' Note that replacing 'if (isTrue()) assert false;' with 'assert isTrue();' may change the program semantics when asserts are disabled if condition has side effects. Use the Ignore 'if' statements with trivial 'assert' option if you want to hide a warning for 'if' statements containing only 'assert' statement in their bodies. Inspection ID: TrivialIf

