Reports cases where the argument of a method call on a 'java.util.Collection' or 'java.util.Map' is the collection or map itself. Such situations may occur as a result of copy-paste in code with raw types. Example: 'ArrayList list = new ArrayList<>();
  list.add(list); // warning here
  return list.hashCode(); // throws StackOverflowError' Inspection ID: CollectionAddedToSelf

Reports unnecessary 'super' qualifiers in method calls and field references. A 'super' qualifier is unnecessary when the field or method of the superclass is not hidden/overridden in the calling class. Example: 'class Foo {
