fullDescription.text:
Reports calls to 'abstract' methods of the current class during object construction. A method is called during object construction if it is inside a: Constructor Non-static instance initializer Non-static field initializer 'clone()' method 'readObject()' method 'readObjectNoData()' method Such calls may result in subtle bugs, as object initialization may happen before the method call. Example: 'abstract class Parent {
    abstract void abstractMethod();
