fullDescription.text:
Reports calls to 'get()' on an 'Optional' without checking that it has a value. Calling 'Optional.get()' on an empty 'Optional' instance will throw an exception. Example: 'void x(List<Integer> list) {
    final Optional<Integer> optional =
      list.stream().filter(x -> x > 10).findFirst();
    final Integer result = optional.get(); // problem here
  }' This inspection depends on the Java feature 'Stream and Optional API', which is available since Java 8. Inspection ID: OptionalGetWithoutIsPresent

