Reports double-checked locking. Double-checked locking tries to initialize a field on demand and in a thread-safe manner, while avoiding the cost of synchronization. Unfortunately it is not thread-safe when used on a field that is not declared 'volatile'. When using Java 1.4 or earlier, double-checked locking doesn't work even with a 'volatile' field. Read the article linked above for a detailed explanation of the problem. Example of incorrect double-checked locking: 'class Foo {
    private Helper helper = null;
    public Helper getHelper() {
      if (helper == null)
        synchronized(this) {
          if (helper == null) helper = new Helper();
        }
        return helper;
      }
    }
    // other functions and members...
  }' Inspection ID: DoubleCheckedLocking

