Inspection ID: UnnecessaryEmptyArrayUsage

fullDescription.text:
Reports creation of 'Boolean' objects. Constructing new 'Boolean' objects is rarely necessary, and may cause performance problems if done often enough. Also, 'Boolean' constructors are deprecated since Java 9 and could be removed or made inaccessible in future Java versions. Example: 'Boolean b1 = new Boolean(true);
  Boolean b2 = new Boolean(str);' After the quick-fix is applied: 'Boolean b1 = Boolean.TRUE;
  Boolean b2 = Boolean.valueOf(str);' Inspection ID: BooleanConstructor

